Note that 3.4.3 lets you open closed doors by clicking on them,
if you happen to be playing with a tileset.  I never would have
noticed that myself (I'm very much a keyboard user), but my dad
was playing with the Qt build, and he didn't really know what
he was doing, so he just sort of started clicking on stuff...
Needless to say he had a high mortality rate, but not for lack
of ability to open doors.

> Could this 'new' "door code" be the 'culprit' for all the
> keyboard differences (and problems)?  I can't understand
> why anything at all got changed with the keyboard set-up

That's explained in the changelogs, IIRC, or maybe it was in the
thread here that announced 4.0.0.  The keyboard code was modified
by necessity as part of the process of separating the I/O layer
from the game engine, in order to enable network transparency.
That's the major change needed in order to allow for the (later)
creation of a web-based UI, among other things.  It was also
long overdue just in general and will allow *proper* support
for different character setups (so that people on different OS
platforms can watch one another's games without seeing ugly
cyrillic gibberish or so forth) down the line.

However, the ^A thing and shop-price issues upthread are bugs.
(Any time you make major code changes there are going to be a
few bugs at first.)


